<title>USA: Xerox unit files $2 bln shelf for debt.</title>
<headline>Xerox unit files $2 bln shelf for debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xerox Credit Corp, a financing arm of Xerox Corp, filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $2 billion in medium-term notes.</p>
<p>Underwriters for the shelf offering are Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, Lehman Brothers, Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, Morgan Stanley Dean Witter and Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
